<h2 id="build">build</h2>
<h3 id="html">HTML</h3>
<pre><code class="language-emacs-lisp">(require 'org-ref-refproc) ;; this is not loaded by default!

(let ((org-export-before-parsing-hook '(org-ref-refproc)))
  (org-open-file (org-html-export-to-html)))
</code></pre>
<h3 id="to-an-org-buffer">To an org buffer</h3>
<pre><code class="language-emacs-lisp">(let ((org-export-before-parsing-hook '(org-ref-refproc)))
   (org-org-export-as-org))
</code></pre>
<h3 id="to-odt">To ODT</h3>
<p>See <a href="https://orgmode.org/manual/LaTeX-math-snippets.html">https://orgmode.org/manual/LaTeX-math-snippets.html</a> for details about the equations. You need these options. I didn’t get the latexml approach to work described there, but this worked somewhat ok.</p>
<pre><code class="language-emacs-lisp">(let ((org-export-before-parsing-hook '(org-ref-refproc)))
  (org-open-file (org-odt-export-to-odt) 'system))
</code></pre>
<h3 id="latex">LaTeX</h3>
<p>It isn’t clear why you would go this route, since org-ref is for LaTeX in the
first place, but this does work nicely.</p>
<pre><code class="language-emacs-lisp">(let ((org-export-before-parsing-hook '(org-ref-refproc)))
  (org-open-file (org-babel-latex-tex-to-pdf (org-latex-export-to-latex))))
</code></pre>
